# Jaypee Parcel Service — the white-label brand for the web app.
#
#   Docker:        docker run --env-file brands/jaypee.env -e AGENT_URL=http://agent:3001 -p 8080:80 rafai-web
#   Dev / static:  cp brands/jaypee.env .env.local && npm run dev        (or: npm run build)
#
# The images are files in brands/jaypee/, named below by their path on the site.
# A build, or the container at start, copies in only the files named here, so
# this customer's site serves its own logo and no one else's. source.png is the
# artwork as supplied; logo.png is it trimmed to 144 px tall at most, twice the
# sidebar's 72 px; icon.png is the tab icon. All are transparent.
#
# Colours are taken from the logo. Its green (#054105) is 11.3:1 against the
# page, so it is the accent as it is; on the dark theme it is 1.5:1 — invisible
# — so the accent there is a brighter green (#0c990c). The bar across the top is
# the logo's own green, and the sidebar is left neutral. The logo is a solid
# green card that reads on either theme, so there is no dark variant. The icon
# is the truck's cab on the same green.
#
# The assistant's OWN name — what it answers when asked who it is — is set on the
# agent service, as tenant "jaypee" in rafai-ai-agent/src/db/tenants.json.

BRAND_NAME=Jaypee AI
BRAND_COMPANY=Jaypee Parcel Service
BRAND_TAGLINE=Analytics
BRAND_ACCENT=054105
BRAND_ACCENT_DARK=0c990c
BRAND_BAR=054105
BRAND_LOGO_URL=/brands/jaypee/logo.png
BRAND_FAVICON_URL=/brands/jaypee/icon.png
